 hand. Therefore, there are two fingers visible in the photo.\", \"To determine how many fingers are visible in the photo, let's analyze the image step by step:\\n\\n1. The person is holding a rectangular object in front of their face.\\n2. The object appears to be held with their fingers.\\n3. Observing the fingers, we can see three distinct fingers: the thumb, index finger, and middle finger.\\n4. The ring finger and pinky are not visible due to the object covering them.\\n\\nBased on this analysis, the number of fingers visible in the photo is three.\\n\\nFinal answer: Three fingers are visible in the photo.\"]", "time_sec": 12.457, "generation_time_seconds": 12.3004, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0001, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 8253, 1246, 1657, 19225, 525, 9434, 304, 279, 6548, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 2168, 4933, 264, 1697, 9963, 264, 6548, 4034, 624, 17, 13, 576, 1697, 594, 1424, 374, 25244, 9434, 11, 11689, 279, 24050, 323, 19225, 9963, 279, 4034, 624, 18, 13, 576, 24050, 374, 9355, 9434, 389, 279, 2115, 3108, 315, 279, 4034, 624, 19, 13, 576, 19225, 9963, 279, 4034, 525, 25244, 95701, 714, 71350, 382, 6025, 16585, 21930, 11, 432, 7952, 429, 2326, 19225, 525, 9434, 304, 279, 6548, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.628, -0.0656, -0.0645, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.9245, -0.0, 0.0, -1.4961, -0.2425, -0.0006, -0.0005, -0.2348, -0.0078, -0.0085, -0.7617, -0.2152, -0.0713, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0043, -0.4178, -0.0053, -0.1201, -0.001, -0.5972, -0.0039, -0.6098, -2.3081, -0.114, -1.2056, -0.0463, -3.6385, -0.0924, -0.0, -0.0292, -0.0001, 0.0, 0.0, -0.5285, -0.9451, -0.2098, -0.0359, -0.0002, -1.1502, -0.0044, -0.0114, -0.0, -0.0105, 0.0, -0.0149, -0.0002, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0411, -0.0494, -0.7381, 0.0, -0.0102, -0.0109, -0.578, -0.3039, -0.7424, -1.5097, -2.2734, -1.1781, -1.9313, -0.1095, -0.2225, -0.6118, -0.2732, -0.1428, -1.491, -0.0, -0.361, -0.0221, -0.6231, -0.0002, -0.0005, -2.2194, -0.5245], "cumulative_logprob": -32