{"id": "329", "question": "How many chimneys are visible in the image?", "gt": "Three; There are three chimneys; I can see three chimneys on top of the house", "pred": "1", "group_key": "visual challenge", "sub_category": "visual challenge", "dataset": "haloquest", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To determine the number of chimneys visible in the image:\n\n1. Scan the entire image for any structures that resemble chimneys.\n2. Focus on the roof of the house, as chimneys are typically located there.\n3. Identify the house in the image and examine its roof.\n4. Count the visible chimneys.\n\nAfter following these steps, I can confirm that there is one chimney visible on the roof of the house.\n\nFinal answer: 1", "cot": "[\"To determine the number of chimneys visible in the image:\\n\\n1. Scan the entire image for any structures that resemble chimneys.\\n2. Focus on the roof of the house, as chimneys are typically located there.\\n3. Identify the house in the image and examine its roof.\\n4. Count the visible chimneys.\\n\\nAfter following these steps, I can confirm that there is one chimney visible on the roof of the house.\\n\\nFinal answer: 1\", \"To determine the number of chimneys visible in the image, I'll follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Scan the entire image for structures that resemble chimneys.\\n2. Focus on the house, as chimneys are typically found there.\\n3. Count each distinct chimney visible.\\n\\nStep 1: Scanning the image, I see a house with a roof.\\nStep 2: Focusing on the house, I notice a structure protruding from the roof that resembles a chimney.\\nStep 3: Counting the distinct chimneys, I see only one on the visible side of the house.\\n\\nFinal answer: 1\", \"To determine the number of chimneys visible in the image, let's analyze it step by step:\\n\\n1. **Identify the structure**: The main structure in the image is a house.\\n2. **Locate the roof**: The roof of the house is visible in the image.\\n3. **Count the chimneys**: Upon examining the